      "writtenOn": "2022-09-13T14:47:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This has already been merged so I can\u0027t update the change. All I can do is explain here.\n\nBasically, we need to do this to associate hidden API flags with the library that provides the class members to which the flags apply so that when we exclude the library from an sdk snapshot we can also exclude the associated flags.\n\nWe already do that implicitly for those flags which are generated from @UnsupportedAppUsage annotations. This extends that to cover flags which are provided outside the source.\n\nLonger term, if we could migrate these flags to use @UnsupportedAppUsage we could remove this mechanism.",
      "parentUuid": "0143eef6_608aaf80",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 9,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "3f1ae0b55acd7e727c6227c3ab3e4f34e885e478",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4f6b8187_3c6bc28c",
        "filename": "java/base.go",
