      "writtenOn": "2022-08-24T15:08:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this adds hiddenapi properties to far more than just `java_sdk_library` -- this will add it to ~all java/android module types -- if only necessary for `java_sdk_library` can you add only there?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 270,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 272,
        "endChar": 28
      },
      "revId": "3f1ae0b55acd7e727c6227c3ab3e4f34e885e478",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "772bb85b_3397219a",
        "filename": "java/base.go",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 272,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-13T14:47:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can also use this in java_library which is why they were added there. The jacocoagent is a java_library which has some associated hidden API packages. We need to conditionally add the library and packages when building a coverage enabled bootclasspath.\n\nAt the moment we have some special code to handle that in `bootclasspath_fragment`. This change will allow the packages to be provided in the `jacocoagent` java_library and so be easily updated if necessary when `jacocoagent` is updated.\n\nThere is a lot of logic in `java_library` and more so in `java_sdk_library` which only applies to libraries which are part of the bootclasspath.\n\nIn the Bazel world I would expect this logic to be handled in special \"java_boot_library\" and \"java_sdk_boot_library\" rules which extend the existing `java_library` and `java_sdk_library` rules.\n\nDoing that in Soong would be very hard because of the fact that so much of the code depends on knowing the exact type of the module and not just on what date it provides.",
      "parentUuid": "4f6b8187_3c6bc28c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 270,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 272,
        "endChar": 28
      },
